  "transcript": "Canonical serialisation rule: JSON with all keys recursively sorted in ascending lexicographic order, no whitespace, no trailing newlines. The proposal artifact (proposal_canon.json) is serialised by this rule to an exact byte sequence; hProposal = sha256(proposal_canon.json) is computed by running sha256sum on that file; the seed is then derived as sha256(hProposal || salt) where hProposal is the hex digest and salt = ca10d248eb54b8093de0cff800fa4c04b7557ec56153258d56598119c44c85e2 is the engine-supplied salt. A third party with the proposal_canon.json file, the salt, and this transcript can reproduce hProposal and the final seed by running sha256sum on the canonical file and then hashing the concatenated digests, arriving at seedHex = 34a1e7bbf6d47cc5ad69a7c6cfdacf3afbedf3516f92f4f5c70de562c8ff8775 deterministically."
